![FOSS4G Group Photo]($images/foss4g-2025-group-photo.jpg)

FOSS4G 2027 in Bristol (23–29 August 2027) will again offer a Travel Grant Programme (TGP) to help community members attend who would otherwise be unable to. This page outlines how the programme is expected to work, based on previous FOSS4G conferences.

**Please note: the dates, grant tiers and application process for FOSS4G 2027 are yet to be confirmed. All details marked TBC below are placeholders and will be updated once the programme opens.**

[Join our Mailing List](https://mailchi.mp/foss4g/mailing-list) to be notified when TGP applications open.

## About the TGP

The [OSGeo FOSS4G Travel Grant Program](https://www.osgeo.org/initiatives/foss4g-travel-grant-program/) was established by the OSGeo Board in 2017 to facilitate accessibility and diversity at global and regional FOSS4G events. The programme is managed by the OSGeo Conference Committee together with each FOSS4G organising team.

The TGP is funded by an annual commitment from the OSGeo Board, sponsor donations, collections at FOSS4G events, and an ongoing crowdfunding campaign. The number of grants available depends on this funding and on the number of applications received.

You can support the programme by [donating to the OSGeo Travel Grant Program](https://www.osgeo.org/initiatives/foss4g-travel-grant-program/).

